{
 "about": "The BBQS identity keys: one normalization rule per key, written once here and implemented identically in SQL (public.kg_*_key and the pairing helpers, created by supabase/migrations/20261117181500_prevent_duplicates.sql, which builds the uq_* indexes on the identity keys), TypeScript (supabase/functions/_shared/identity-keys.ts, what the write paths look up by) and Python (kg/identity_keys.py, what kg/quality.py and the exporter use). Every implementation must return `want` for every vector: kg/ci_check.py checks Python, tests/guards/identity-normalization.test.mjs checks TypeScript, and the migration's self-test block (keys-02, generated from this file) checks Postgres when it is applied. tests/guards/kg-identity-keys.test.mjs keeps the LinkML unique_keys, the SHACL shapes, kg/quality.py and the migration in step with this file; tests/guards/kg-resource-links-parity.test.mjs does the same for resource_link_predicates.",
 "conventions": {
  "whitespace": "ASCII only: space, \\t, \\n, \\v, \\f, \\r. 'trim' strips these at both ends.",
  "case": "ASCII only: A-Z <-> a-z; every other character is left as it is (Postgres COLLATE \"C\").",
  "null": "null/None/NULL means the value has no key: it is neither enforced nor matched."
 },
 "layers": {
  "sql": "the function the database computes the key with; the uq_* expression unique index in `db` is built on it",
  "ts": "the function in supabase/functions/_shared/identity-keys.ts",
  "py": "the function in kg/identity_keys.py",
  "db": "the table, column and unique index that refuse a second row with the same key",
  "linkml": "the unique_keys entry in kg/bbqs.linkml.yaml (gen-owl: owl:hasKey)",
  "shape": "the SHACL shape in kg/shapes/validation.shapes.ttl that finds two nodes with the same exact value in an export",
  "quality": "the identifier kg/quality.py duplicates() folds with this key (its FOLD map)"
 },
